# Upstream baseline for the mainline H5000M build.
#
# WHY openwrt/openwrt main (SNAPSHOT) AND NOT 25.12
# -------------------------------------------------
# Hiveton H5000M support was added upstream by
#   6487cc9a1f  "mediatek: add support for Hiveton H5000M"   (2026-01-09)
# and that commit is only on `main`.  Verified against the published images:
#
#   releases/25.12.0 .. 25.12.5 -> profiles.json contains NO hiveton_h5000m
#   snapshots/                  -> profiles.json contains hiveton_h5000m
#
# The openwrt-25.12 *branch* head does carry the device (cherry-picked after
# the 25.12.5 tag), but no released 25.12.x image does, so SNAPSHOT `main` is
# simultaneously the newest and the only mainline upstream that ships H5000M
# firmware today.  It is also what every in-tree plugin for this board is
# verified against (luci-app-h5000m-fancontrol: "OpenWrt SNAPSHOT";
# ddimension feed: `stable/snapshot/aarch64_cortex-a53`).
#
# Set OPENWRT_REPO_BRANCH=openwrt-25.12 to build the 25.12 branch instead once
# 25.12.6 ships the device.
OPENWRT_REPO_URL=https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt.git
OPENWRT_REPO_BRANCH=main

# Reproducible baseline.  Two different facts live in this block and they are
# NOT the same fact:
#
#   * the revision the PATCH STACK is aligned to — the one
#     scripts/verify-upstream-integration.sh verifies every patch against;
#   * the last revision a FULL BUILD (image + apk repository + all three publish
#     gates) was observed to pass on.
#
# They coincided at 0f8cceb, then stopped coinciding when mainline bumped
# nftables 1.1.6 -> 1.1.7 and libnftnl 1.3.1 -> 1.3.2 between 0f8cceb and 99426e4
# (both fullcone userspace patches had to be regenerated — see
# install_nftables_patches), and they coincide again at 058da17 below.
#
# 2026-11-17 upstream-sync review: 99426e4 -> 058da17
# ---------------------------------------------------
# 058da17 is the revision the 2026-11-16 scheduled build actually built and
# passed with every gate (image + apk repository + attestation + publish +
# Pages), so it satisfies both halves at once.  What the 1074 upstream commits
# between 99426e4 and that build did, and did not, touch:
#
#   * nftables 1.1.7-r1 and libnftnl 1.3.2-r1 — UNCHANGED, so
#     nftables-patches/100-fullcone-expression.patch and
#     libnftnl-patches/100-fullnftl-expression.patch apply byte-for-byte as
#     before.  Nothing to regenerate.
#   * firewall4 — its source commit moved b6e5157 -> 3722ead ("firewall4: update
#     to Git HEAD (2026-11-08)", which is `main`'s 3722ead as of this review).
#     firewall4-patches/100-fullcone-support.patch touches
#     templates/ruleset.uc, templates/zone-masq.uc and ucode/fw4.uc, so it had to
#     be re-checked: `git apply --check` against 3722ead passes, and the 11-16
#     build is the proof that it also applies inside the real build.
#   * kernel — still 6.18.60 (LINUX_VERSION-6.18 = .60); the 11-16 build reported
#     kernel_abi=ac7024928df204cd6201adcbc2974cb5 for it.
#
# 2026-11-23 upstream-sync review: 058da17 -> 14a07b7 (108 commits, NOT yet
# promoted to the pin — see the last paragraph of this block)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the 108 commits do and do not touch:
#
#   * nftables (1.1.7), libnftnl (1.3.2) and firewall4 (source 3722ead) — all
#     UNCHANGED.  scripts/verify-upstream-integration.sh --ref 14a07b7 passes
#     all four userspace layers (nftables, libnftnl, firewall4, mt76) plus both
#     tree patches and every Nikki-RS anchor and clash-rs hash pin.
#   * kernel 6.18.60 -> 6.18.64 (f7d14dc28 -> a5383abb3 -> 75fde714f).  The
#     kernel ABI moves with it, which is exactly why the kmods and the pinned
#     sing-box live in the image / this project's repository and not upstream.
#   * toolchain: gcc 15 becomes the default (fd3b9d467).  This is the one change
#     in the range that can break a package build for reasons unrelated to our
#     patches, so it needs a real build, not a patch dry-run.  Half of it was
#     cleared on 2026-11-23 by compiling the two pieces that can be built in
#     isolation under gcc 15.3.0: the patched libnftnl 1.3.2 + nftables 1.1.7
#     (inside `verify-upstream-integration.sh --compile`) and the out-of-tree
#     local-packages/nft-fullcone module against 6.18.64 headers, which still
#     carries `-Werror -Wall` and compiles clean.  The image itself is the part
#     that remains unproven.
#   * netfilter.mk: added kmod-nf-xtables and *_LEGACY symbols, and rewired
#     kmod-ipt-*/kmod-nft-compat to depend on it.  Additive; the kmod list here
#     gets the new dependency through kconfig automatically.
#   * mediatek target: only mt7981/mt7986 DTS and base-files changed.  The
#     hiveton_h5000m DTS and the two patches/ hunks are untouched.
#
# Deliberately a fixed revision, not "whatever main's head is": `latest` is the
# mode that follows the branch head; this is the reproducible one.  Bumping it is
# therefore a review action with evidence attached (a build that passed), not a
# scheduled edit.
#
# Why a pin cannot just chase main every day: a patch regenerated against
# nftables 1.1.7 cannot be applied to 1.1.6 — 1.1.7 added `<*>` start-condition
# prefixes to the NAT keyword rules in src/scanner.l — so a pin whose value
# tracks a moving target is not a pin.
#
# The patch-stack half is machine-verified by
# scripts/verify-upstream-integration.sh (also a PR gate); the full-build half is
# recorded as a separate sentence here rather than being allowed to blur into it.
#
# So the pin moved off 058da17 on 2026-11-24, but not to 14a07b7: main had
# already advanced to ce245c8 by then, and that is the revision the 2026-11-24
# build actually assembled.
#
# 2026-11-24 pin promotion: 058da17 -> ce245c873917cfbb412244dad80e395effed3167
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI run 45307537181 (dispatched on 28ae754 with `pinned=false`, i.e. the
# `latest` line) built exactly ce245c8 — BUILD-INFO.txt records
# `openwrt_revision=ce245c873917cfbb412244dad80e395effed3167`,
# `openwrt_version_code=r0-ce245c8`, `project_version=1.3.0` — and passed every
# assembled-image check:
#
#   * `Verify the fullcone chain is really in the image` — the out-of-tree
#     nft_fullcone module is in the image and the kmod list still resolves.
#   * `Verify the proxy stack dependencies are in the image`
#   * `Verify the built repository can satisfy every frontend on its own`
#   * `Audit build warnings`, plus the apk repository published to Pages
#     (281.2 MB) and the rootfs test harness (real `uci` under qemu-user)
#     running against the rootfs of that very build.
#
# That is the "image + apk repository" half of the rule above.  `publish` was
# switched off for that run on purpose (it would have replaced the assets of the
# already-released 1.3.0 with a different tree under the same version number);
# the publish step does not depend on the upstream revision and was last
# exercised green by run 45189136209.  `gcc 15` being the default since
# fd3b9d467 is covered by this build: it is the assembled image, not a dry run.
#
# Cost of a bump, measured on that run: 202 min total, of which 170 min is
# Build — every cache key is revision-scoped, so a new revision pays a full
# rebuild (the same job takes 20 min in Build when the revision is unchanged).
#
# Move the pin to 14a07b78e9ac9d604547533550e6aa41955ac588 (snapshot r0-14a07b7)
# only if that specific revision ever needs reproducing; it is behind ce245c8, so
# normal builds already contain its content.  firewall4/mt76 used to be
# "unverifiable on Windows" (the snapshots contain symlinks tar cannot create
# there); run the verifier in a Linux container when you need all four layers
# judged — the script now prints the exact command when it detects that tar
# failure.
#
# Used when OPENWRT_TRACK=pinned, and recorded as the fallback baseline in
# BUILD-INFO.txt when tracking `latest`.
#
# The kernel ABI moves between snapshots that both call themselves 6.18.x
# (3a22303 -> 8ae0a62b, 0f8cceb -> f3b7e5e1), which is why the kmods and the
# pinned sing-box ship inside the image and in this project's own repository
# rather than being fetched from the official snapshot.
# 2026-11-24 pin promotion: ce245c8 -> 727d8d2f8e5b19a2121e2cf05824e9e5cac35310
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI run 45436214328 (dispatched on 694667a with `pinned=false`, i.e. the
# `latest` line) built exactly 727d8d2 — BUILD-INFO.txt records
# `openwrt_revision=727d8d2f8e5b19a2121e2cf05824e9e5cac35310`,
# `openwrt_version_code=r0-727d8d2`, `upstream_track=latest` — and passed
# every assembled-image check the ce245c8 promotion passed, plus
# `Publish release` that this time stayed on:
#
#   * `Verify the fullcone chain is really in the image`
#   * `Verify the proxy stack dependencies are in the image`
#   * `Verify the built repository can satisfy every frontend on its own`
#   * `Audit build warnings`, `Attest the firmware and the apk repository`,
#     the apk repository published to Pages, and the rootfs harness
#     (`设备脚本测试`) green against the rootfs of that very build.
#
# What moved between the two revisions is not this board: the 11 upstream
# commits are realtek/airoha/starfive targets plus a ppp `options.pptp` fix.
# No mediatek target file, no `package/kernel/mt76` — so the two patches this
# project carries (`0001-h5000m-userspace-fan-control.patch`,
# `0002-h5000m-mt76-txwi-fix.patch`) still apply untouched, which is exactly
# what the promotion rule asks for.
#
# Cost, measured: 41.8 min total with `Build` at 12.9 min, because the build
# cache restored through its restore-keys fallback (9.5 min).  The 170-minute
# `Build` recorded for the 058da17 -> ce245c8 promotion was a cold cache, so the
# price of a bump is cache-dependent, not a constant to budget for.
#
# --- 2026-11-25 promotion: 727d8d2 -> fb742de8 -------------------------------
#
# The evidence for this one is the 1.4.0 release build itself, not a rehearsal:
# release-please merged `chore(master): release 1.4.0`, tagged `v1.4.0` and ran
# `gh workflow run build.yml --ref v1.4.0` (run 45618943712), which built
# fb742de8e5126809fddf16fa2b5e82b016be0edb with everything green —
# `Verify the fullcone chain …`, `Verify the proxy stack dependencies …`,
# `Verify the built repository can satisfy every frontend on its own`,
# `Audit build warnings` (`No warnings about packages this project builds.`),
# `Attest the firmware and the apk repository`, `Publish release` (7 assets),
# the apk repository deployed to Pages, and `设备脚本测试` against that rootfs.
#
# That build shipped to users as v1.4.0, so THE PIN HAS TO MOVE TO IT: leaving
# the pin at 727d8d2 would mean `pinned=true` builds no longer reproduce the
# release that exists on the releases page.  The delta is 10 commits / 37 files
# — realtek, qualcommax, airoha, loongarch64, bcm27xx, plus 20 `generic: 6.18`
# patches.  The only mediatek file is `package/boot/uboot-mediatek/Makefile`
# (an image-builder chainloader, not this target), there is **no**
# `package/kernel/mt76` and **no** ppp file, so the two patches this project
# carries (`0001-h5000m-userspace-fan-control.patch`,
# `0002-h5000m-mt76-txwi-fix.patch`) still apply untouched — and the build
# above is the proof, not the inference.
#
# Side note worth keeping: the tag build ran with `pinned` defaulted to false
# (release-please passes no inputs), so `BUILD-INFO.txt` of 1.4.0 honestly says
# `upstream_track=latest` / `openwrt_revision=fb742de8…`.  A `pinned=true`
# build from now on resolves to the same sha, so both tracks agree until
# upstream moves again.
# 2026-11-26 promotion: fb742de8 -> 9285edcb（候选构建已证明）
#
# 与上一次不同的地方：这次先构建候选、再动 pin。  上一次是发布构建本身充当了
# 演练，因为发布用的是分支头。  这次 run 45664615331（`pinned=false`，因此解析
# 到当时的 refs/heads/main）用 `9285edcb` 跑完整流程：`构建固件`、`发布 apk
# 仓库`、`设备脚本测试` 全绿，`Verify the fullcone chain is really in the image`、
# `Verify the proxy stack dependencies are in the image`、`Verify the built
# repository can satisfy every frontend on its own`、`Audit build warnings`
# 全部通过，BUILD-INFO 记的是 `openwrt_revision=9285edcb…` /
# `openwrt_version_code=r0-9285edc` / `kernel_version=6.18.64` /
# `kernel_abi=ac7024928df204cd6201adcbc2974cb5`（与 1.4.0 同一个 ABI），
# 并且 feed 段只剩 6 条真实 feed —— 修复前的 `feed_base=` 与 `feed_*.tmp=`
# 那些假行没有了，说明 record_feed_revisions 的 `.git` 判据在真实 CI 里生效。
#
# 相对 fb742de8 的差异是 8 个 commit / 13 个文件，全部落在 realtek
# （`target/linux/realtek/files-6.18/drivers/{net/dsa/rtl83xx,soc/realtek}`）与
# `target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/759-*`/`760-*`（MxL862xx DSA 标签）。
# 没有 mediatek 目标文件、没有 `package/kernel/mt76`、没有 ppp，所以本项目的
# 两个补丁（`0001-h5000m-userspace-fan-control.patch`、
# `0002-h5000m-mt76-txwi-fix.patch`）不受影响 —— 上面那次构建就是证据。
#
# 现在 `latest` 与 `pinned` 再次收敛到同一个 sha，直到上游再动。
#
# 2026-11-26 promotion: 9285edcb -> e50f7f96（候选构建已证明）
#
# run 45735538170（`pinned=false`，ref `master`@`fae0112`）解析到
# `e50f7f9651b9bd635e2d75f4f4789768af20f8dd` 并完整跑绿：31 分钟，`构建固件`、
# `发布 apk 仓库`（含 Pages 部署）、`设备脚本测试（复用工作流）` 三个 job 全 success，
# `Verify the fullcone chain is really in the image`、
# `Verify the proxy stack dependencies are in the image`、
# `Verify the built repository can satisfy every frontend on its own`、
# `Audit build warnings`（`No warnings about packages this project builds.`）全部通过。
# BUILD-INFO：`openwrt_revision=e50f7f96…` / `openwrt_version_code=r0-e50f7f9` /
# `kernel_version=6.18.64` / `kernel_abi=ac7024928df204cd6201adcbc2974cb5`，
# **ABI 与 1.4.2 完全相同**，所以已发布的 apk 仓库不需要重建兼容性说明。
#
# 相对 9285edcb 只有 2 个 commit / 4 个文件：
#
#   * `package/firmware/linux-firmware/Makefile` 20261019 -> 20261124（PKG_HASH 随之改变）；
#   * `package/firmware/linux-firmware/qca_ath11k.mk`：`ath11k-firmware-qca2066` 的
#     install 从 `$(INSTALL_DATA)` 改成 `$(CP)`。本板是 mediatek/filogic（MT7988），
#     不带 ath11k 固件，所以这两处对镜像无影响；它们唯一的作用是让 dl 缓存里的
#     `linux-firmware-20261124.tar.xz` 成为一个新下载项。
#   * `package/network/services/dnsmasq/Makefile` PKG_RELEASE 12 -> 13，加
#     `patches/300-ubus-add-lease-methods.patch`（409 行，新增 ubus lease 方法）。
#     本工程的 `dnsmasq-full` 走的就是这个包，但没有本地补丁压在上面，
#     所以不存在 rebase；上面那次构建已经把 dnsmasq-full + 该补丁一起编过。
#     没有 `package/kernel/mt76`、没有 ppp、没有 nftables/libnftnl/firewall4，
#     所以本项目的四个补丁链（fan-control、mt76-txwi、fullcone 三件套）一字未动。
#
# 为什么这次可以推 pin：这 2 个 commit 里没有一条会改 kernel ABI 或 fullcone 依赖，
# 而候选构建把三条 `Verify …` 都跑过了 —— 与上一次相同的证据标准，不是推断。
#
# `${VAR:-…}` on purpose: a candidate bump is proved by building that exact
# commit FIRST — `scripts/local-build.sh --revision <sha>`, or the
# OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION repository variable in CI, which `build.yml` forwards —
# and only a revision whose image + apk repository + publish all passed is
# recorded here.  Editing this line to an unproven commit is the thing the
# override exists to avoid.
OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION=${OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION:-e50f7f9651b9bd635e2d75f4f4789768af20f8dd}
# Must describe OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION: its first seven hex characters are the
# tail of this label (`r0-e50f7f9`), and write_build_info() drops the label when
# the two disagree.  A bump therefore updates both lines.
OPENWRT_PINNED_SNAPSHOT=${OPENWRT_PINNED_SNAPSHOT:-r0-e50f7f9}

# `latest` (default) follows the branch head on every build — that is the point
# of a scheduled auto-build.  `pinned` builds OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION so a build
# can be reproduced exactly; scripts/local-build.sh --pinned selects it.
OPENWRT_TRACK=latest

# Target triple, as published by OpenWrt.
OPENWRT_TARGET=mediatek
OPENWRT_SUBTARGET=filogic
OPENWRT_PROFILE=hiveton_h5000m
OPENWRT_ARCH=aarch64_cortex-a53
OPENWRT_IMAGE_PREFIX=openwrt-mediatek-filogic-hiveton_h5000m

# Optional fallback modem stack.  luci-app-mt5700m (the FAN789 panel for the
# built-in MT5700M) hard-depends on `ubus-at-daemon` and `sms-tool_q`, and both
# are packaged only by the QModem feed.  write_feeds_conf() therefore appends
# this feed *only* when ENABLE_MT5700M=true; a wwand build never sees it, since
# the two stacks are mutually exclusive and QModem brings its own drivers.
QMODEM_REPO_URL=https://github.com/FUjr/QModem.git
QMODEM_REPO_BRANCH=main
